In article <3478.27359c0c@cc.nu.oz.au> c8730752@cc.nu.oz.au writes:
>I would like so see( this must have been talked about before), a "hunger
>meter" and a "weight meter". Sometimes you are asked if you want to stop
>eating sometimes you aren't! The present indicator of hunger is quite 
>difficult to judge, unless you start timing your steps!
>Also, what about picking a limited number of items off the floor of the same 
>kind, eg, 1 of 2 orcs corpses. Even if I have the strenght to lift one, 
>the computer will try to pick up both which I don't have strenght for.

There is a "hunger meter".  If you are not satiated when you eat, you will
not choke.

There is a "weight meter".  If you pick up something when close to your
maximum, you will get told that you have a little trouble lifting it.

If there are 2 orc corpses and you can only lift one, the computer will
let you pick the one up.
